# helix training image: the pimm environment, corrected.
#
# Built FROM youngsam's pimm image rather than from scratch, because that image
# carries a large amount of CUDA work worth keeping -- torch 2.10+cu126 and the
# prebuilt torch_scatter / torch_sparse / spconv / flash-attn wheels that cannot
# be compiled on a login node with no CUDA toolkit.
#
# It fixes exactly two things, both of which were live defects:
#
#   1. pimm_data was baked in at 0.3.0 -- which still REGISTERS AddNoise and
#      Digitize. helix registers both of those now, so the stale copy plus a
#      current helix double-registers and pimm_data/_registry.py raises KeyError.
#      The boundary move is lockstep and this image was on the wrong side of it.
#
#      It is also why configs/pimm/coeff_fm_train.py carries an elaborate
#      sys.path.insert(1) dance: the comment there says the checkout "has to WIN
#      over site-packages, not merely be present". With the right version
#      installed, that requirement disappears.
#
#   2. PyWavelets was absent, so this image could not run helix's DSP at all and
#      a SECOND image was needed just to build corpora. One correct image does
#      both.
#
# What is deliberately NOT baked in: pimm and helix themselves. They are the code
# under active development and arrive by bind mount / PYTHONPATH, so a change to
# either does not need an image rebuild. Only DEPENDENCIES are installed here.
#
# Build. Needs no root and no sibling checkout -- run it from anywhere, on any
# cluster, with outbound network to ghcr.io and github.com:
#
#   APPTAINER_TMPDIR=$LSCRATCH apptainer build --fakeroot \
#     <somewhere>/helix-train.sif container/helix-train.def
#
# It used to require the parent directory holding BOTH this checkout and a
# pimm-data checkout side by side, because pimm-data arrived through %files.
# That is gone: the revision is pinned below and fetched from git.
#
# Rebuild whenever PIMM_DATA_REV changes, and move it in step with helix -- the
# image is half of the lockstep pair.

Bootstrap: docker
# pimm's OWN published image, pinned by DIGEST.
#
# This used to be `Bootstrap: localimage` from
# /sdf/data/neutrino/youngsam/images/pimm_v0.5.1.sif -- an absolute path into
# another user's directory on one cluster. That made this file unbuildable
# anywhere else, which is fatal for a handover: the base is 8.9 GB, is not ours
# to redistribute, and its only provenance was an md5 of a local file that a
# second site cannot check.
#
# ghcr.io/deeplearnphysics/pimm publishes the same versions and is pullable
# anonymously (verified 2026-09-17: token 200, manifest 200). The digest below
# is v0.5.1, the version the local .sif carried:
#
#   v0.5.1  sha256:c0dc5a64797d7176d8fc11c3cae5749008f5c6803d69e012f770d927b7a776bf
#   v0.5.2  sha256:bf0623db2982c68489ad8c9ed19edff1b822c4e0fcb482551422641ab8ddc586
#
# By DIGEST, not by tag: a tag can be repointed, which is the same failure the
# `pimm-latest.sif` symlink had. A digest cannot, so two builds of this file
# anywhere in the world share a base byte for byte.
#
# Needs outbound network to ghcr.io at build time. On a site without it, pull
# once where there is network and `apptainer build` from the local .sif.
From: ghcr.io/deeplearnphysics/pimm@sha256:c0dc5a64797d7176d8fc11c3cae5749008f5c6803d69e012f770d927b7a776bf

%arguments
    # Which jax to install. The image is otherwise identical either way.
    #
    #   cuda12  GPU jax. Needs NO GPU to build -- the wheels are prebuilt and
    #           arch-generic (PTX + SASS for sm_70..sm_90), so an image built on
    #           a CPU node or a Turing node runs on Ampere unchanged. This is
    #           the default because helix HAS a jax GPU DSP backend and an image
    #           that cannot use it makes `--backend jax` a lie.
    #   cpu     no CUDA jax. Smaller, and the right choice if the %post guard
    #           below ever fires on your resolver.
    #
    #   apptainer build --build-arg JAX_EXTRA=cpu <out>.sif container/helix-train.def
    JAX_EXTRA=cuda12

%post
    set -e
    VENV=/opt/pimm/.venv
    UV=/usr/local/uv/bin/uv

    # uv installs by hardlinking out of its cache, and in the build sandbox
    # those links do not materialise: a cached package "installs" in 99 ms and
    # then imports as ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pywt.version'.
    # link-mode=copy fixes that. The cache itself is put INSIDE the sandbox, so
    # every build starts with an empty one -- which is what the earlier
    # UV_NO_CACHE=1 was really reaching for, and it is the better way to get it:
    # disabling the cache made uv re-extract into TMPDIR on every invocation and
    # the build then died partway through on the largest package.
    export UV_LINK_MODE=copy
    export UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uvcache

    # TMPDIR is INHERITED from whoever runs `apptainer build`, and inside the
    # build sandbox that path usually does not exist: on this cluster it is
    # $LSCRATCH/..., bind-mounted for `apptainer exec` but NOT for %post. uv
    # writes its interpreter-probe module there, so the probe vanishes and uv
    # dies with
    #
    #   Failed to inspect Python interpreter ...
    #   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'python.get_interpreter_info'
    #
    # which reads like a broken interpreter and is nothing of the kind. Pinning
    # it makes the build independent of the builder's environment, which is the
    # whole point of this file now.
    export TMPDIR=/tmp
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" "$UV_CACHE_DIR"
    df -h /tmp | tail -1

    # pimm-data by PINNED REVISION, from the public repo -- not from a
    # side-by-side checkout via %files. The old form required the builder to
    # have a sibling working tree and baked whatever happened to be in it,
    # which is unreproducible by construction and impossible on a fresh
    # machine. This rev is the one coeff-fm's pyproject.toml pins, and the two
    # must move together: the AddNoise/Digitize registration is LOCKSTEP with
    # helix, and an environment that straddles the boundary move raises
    # KeyError on the second registration.
    PIMM_DATA_REV=2b20573ca14f1d06bcc40df8ee8c4e38b13fd94a

    # Replace the stale 0.3.0 rather than shadow it. An editable .pth or a
    # PYTHONPATH entry would leave two copies resolvable and make which one wins
    # depend on sys.path order -- exactly the fragility this image exists to end.
    # Delete any stale build tree BEFORE installing. setuptools copies sources
    # into build/lib and never prunes, so a build/ left from before the forward
    # model moved re-ships every module that was deleted since. It did: the
    # previous image had pimm_data.{noise,noise_jax,coeff,coeff_verify} and
    # readers.coeff_tpc importable, and that coeff_verify was an OLDER copy
    # missing the source_root gap fix (74cfe5f) -- silently wrong answers from a
    # module that is supposed to be gone. build/ is gitignored, so it is
    # invisible to every check that looks at the repo.
    $UV pip uninstall --python $VENV/bin/python pimm-data || true
    $UV pip install --python $VENV/bin/python --no-deps \
        "pimm-data @ git+https://github.com/OmarAlterkait/pimm-data@${PIMM_DATA_REV}" 

    # ONE install for everything else. It was four separate uv invocations,
    # each re-resolving and re-extracting; the build died partway through the
    # last of them. One call also means one consistent resolution.
    #
    #   PyWavelets  helix's DSP half -- its only dep not already here.
    #   pytest      because the first thing anyone does with a new environment
    #               is ask whether it works, and the base image has no runner.
    #   jax         {{ JAX_EXTRA }} -- see %arguments. The hazard is NOT the
    #               GPU: it is that torch 2.10+cu126 brings 16 nvidia-*-cu12
    #               wheels (cudnn 9.10.2.21, cublas 12.6.4.1, ...) and a CUDA
    #               jax depends on the same wheel family. If the resolver moves
    #               any of them to satisfy jax, torch is the thing that breaks,
    #               six hours into a training run. So the versions are captured
    #               before and compared after, and a move FAILS THE BUILD.
    #
    #               `cuda12_local` is not an option here: it wants a system
    #               cuDNN and this image has none -- /usr/local/cuda has the
    #               runtime and nvcc, but libcudnn arrives only as torch's pip
    #               wheel.
    $VENV/bin/python - <<'PYSNAP' > /tmp/nvidia_before.txt
import importlib.metadata as m
for d in sorted(m.distributions(), key=lambda d: d.metadata["Name"] or ""):
    n = d.metadata["Name"] or ""
    if n.startswith("nvidia-") or n in ("torch",):
        print(n, d.version)
PYSNAP
    cat /tmp/nvidia_before.txt

    $UV pip install --python $VENV/bin/python \
        PyWavelets pytest pytest-benchmark "jax[{{ JAX_EXTRA }}]"

    $VENV/bin/python - <<'PYSNAP' > /tmp/nvidia_after.txt
import importlib.metadata as m
for d in sorted(m.distributions(), key=lambda d: d.metadata["Name"] or ""):
    n = d.metadata["Name"] or ""
    if n.startswith("nvidia-") or n in ("torch",):
        print(n, d.version)
PYSNAP
    # Compare only what existed BEFORE. An ADDITION is fine and expected:
    # jax[cuda12] brings its own nvidia-cuda-nvcc-cu12 (12.9) for ptxas, beside
    # torch's 12.6 runtime, and touches nothing torch resolved. What must never
    # happen is a package torch already had being MOVED or REMOVED to satisfy
    # jax -- that breaks torch, six hours into a training run, far from here.
    # The first version of this guard failed on the addition and would have
    # forced jax[cpu] for no reason.
    $VENV/bin/python - <<'PYGUARD'
def read(p):
    return dict(l.split() for l in open(p) if l.strip())
before, after = read("/tmp/nvidia_before.txt"), read("/tmp/nvidia_after.txt")
moved = {k: (v, after.get(k)) for k, v in before.items() if after.get(k) != v}
added = sorted(set(after) - set(before))
if added:
    print("  jax added (fine):", ", ".join(f"{k} {after[k]}" for k in added))
if moved:
    for k, (was, now) in sorted(moved.items()):
        print(f"  MOVED {k}: {was} -> {now}")
    raise SystemExit(
        "FATAL: installing jax[{{ JAX_EXTRA }}] moved a package torch had "
        "pinned.\n"
        "       Rebuild with --build-arg JAX_EXTRA=cpu, or pin jax to a "
        "release whose nvidia-* requirements match torch 2.10+cu126.")
print("  torch's own CUDA wheels: unchanged")
PYGUARD

    df -h /tmp | tail -1
    rm -rf "$UV_CACHE_DIR"

    # Fail the BUILD, not a training run six hours in.
    $VENV/bin/python - <<'PYCHECK'
import pywt, pimm_data
from pimm_data.transform import TRANSFORMS
names = set(TRANSFORMS.module_dict)
assert tuple(int(x) for x in pimm_data.__version__.split(".")[:2]) >= (0, 4), \
    f"stale pimm_data {pimm_data.__version__}"  # tuple, not string: "0.10" < "0.4" lexically
assert "Densify" in names, "pimm_data lost Densify"
for gone in ("AddNoise", "Digitize"):
    assert gone not in names, f"pimm_data still registers {gone}: lockstep violated"
import pytest as _pt, jax as _jx, torch as _t, importlib.util as _iu
# NOT asserting a GPU is visible: this image is built on whatever node is free,
# usually one with no GPU at all, and the jax wheels are arch-generic so the
# build node's hardware says nothing about where it will run.
_jxk = "{{ JAX_EXTRA }}"

# Modules the boundary move DELETED. The registry check above cannot see these:
# they register nothing, so it passed while the image shipped all five.
for _gone in ("pimm_data.noise", "pimm_data.noise_jax", "pimm_data.coeff",
              "pimm_data.coeff_verify", "pimm_data.readers.coeff_tpc"):
    assert _iu.find_spec(_gone) is None, (
        f"{_gone} was deleted from pimm-data but is installed -- a stale "
        f"build/lib leaked into the wheel")
print(f"OK: pywt {pywt.__version__}, pimm_data {pimm_data.__version__}, "
      f"pytest {_pt.__version__}, jax {_jx.__version__} ({_jxk}), "
      f"torch {_t.__version__}, {len(names)} transforms, "
      f"forward model absent as expected")
PYCHECK

%labels
    helix.purpose  corpus building and FM training in one image
    helix.base     ghcr.io/deeplearnphysics/pimm v0.5.1
    helix.base_digest sha256:c0dc5a64797d7176d8fc11c3cae5749008f5c6803d69e012f770d927b7a776bf
    helix.jax      {{ JAX_EXTRA }}

%help
    One image for both halves of the helix workflow.

      corpus:  apptainer exec -B /sdf <img> python scripts/build_coeff_corpus.py ...
      train:   see launch/coeff_fm_train.sbatch

    pimm and helix are NOT installed here; they come from binds/PYTHONPATH.
    pimm-data IS installed, and must match helix -- the AddNoise/Digitize
    registration is lockstep across the two.
